Live-test the reasoning_effort wire against a real vLLM server. Gated on TEST_LANGERTHA_VLLM_URL (existing) plus a reasoning model name (TEST_LANGERTHA_VLLM_REASONING_MODEL).

Wire reality to verify (per vLLM docs https://docs.vllm.ai/en/latest/features/reasoning_outputs/):
- reasoning_effort=low|medium|high emits enable_thinking=true in chat template
- reasoning_effort=none emits enable_thinking=false
- Server MUST be started with --reasoning-parser <qwen3|deepseek_r1|...> matching the loaded model
- Response includes reasoning_content (when model emits it) accessible via Langertha::Response->thinking or similar

Scope: small new file t/88_live_vllm_reasoning.t modeled after t/87_live_vllm_hook.t (skip_all without env var). Should:
1. Send a hard problem (e.g. 'solve 7 factorial step by step') with reasoning_effort=high
2. Assert response non-empty
3. Assert reasoning_content present when --reasoning-parser is set
4. Cross-check with reasoning_effort=none to confirm non-thinking path works

Off the table for this ticket: model-gated capability refinement (capability currently engine-wide; some vLLM models do not honor reasoning_effort). Filed as a separate follow-up if real users hit it.

